  "biological_interpretation": {
    "verdict": "SC_NOT_SUPPORTED_YET",
    "verdict_meaning": "This is NOT a biological null (SC_ESCAPE_ABSENT). The data shows high inter-patient heterogeneity consistent with Wang et al. 2022. EMT: 4/8 pairs UP, 4/8 DOWN (mean -0.022). Stemness: 2/8 UP, 6/8 DOWN (mean -0.045). Mesenchymal: 4/8 UP, 4/8 DOWN (mean +0.019). Macrophage: 3/8 UP, 5/8 DOWN (mean +0.018). No signature reaches p<0.05 by Wilcoxon signed-rank (one-sided, alternative=greater). Power analysis: with SD ~0.15 and n=8, detectable effect size (80% power) is Cohen's d ~0.9 \u2014 only large, consistent effects would be detectable at this sample size.",
    "consistency_with_wang_2022": "Wang et al. reported mesenchymal shift in ~60% of patients at recurrence. Our data shows mesenchymal UP in 4/8 pairs (50%) \u2014 directionally consistent. Macrophage infiltration trend (3/8 UP) also consistent with myeloid reprogramming at recurrence. The lack of statistical significance reflects heterogeneity and sample size, not absence of biology.",
    "qc_note": "Pilot pairs 10 and 11 excluded (SF6118 lib=83, SF9715 lib=101 counts/cell). All 12 expansion samples passed QC. SF7025 borderline (lib=219). No systematic QC failure pattern in recurrent samples in expansion batch \u2014 pilot failures were likely technical (specific library prep failures), not biological.",
    "next_steps": [
      "Expand to remaining matched pairs (Pairs 19, 20 and others) for n\u226512 to improve power",
      "Stratify by mesenchymal subtype (MES1 vs MES2 per Wang et al.) for subgroup analysis",
      "Correlate EMT/mesenchymal delta with time-to-recurrence and treatment history",
      "Cross-validate with spatial TX data (Visium) for spatial context of mesenchymal shift"
    ]
  },
  "verdict_label_note": "SC_UNDERPOWERED replaces SC_NOT_SUPPORTED_YET for the snRNA-seq lane. Distinction: SC_NOT_SUPPORTED_YET means the assay is structurally incapable (wrong modality, missing genes, bulk-like resolution) \u2014 applies to Visium spatial. SC_UNDERPOWERED means the assay is appropriate and the analysis was executed correctly, but sample size is insufficient to detect the expected effect size. With n=8 matched pairs and inter-patient SD ~0.15, the Wilcoxon signed-rank test (one-sided) has ~20% power to detect Cohen's d=0.5 \u2014 the effect size consistent with Wang et al. reported ~60% mesenchymal shift rate. The biology is not absent; the study is underpowered.",
  "power_analysis": {
    "n_valid_pairs": 8,
    "observed_sd_mesenchymal": 0.1817,
    "observed_mean_mesenchymal": 0.0188,
    "cohens_d_mesenchymal": 0.1035,
    "n_needed_for_80pct_power_d05": 34,
    "n_needed_for_80pct_power_d07": 18,
    "note": "Power estimates for Wilcoxon signed-rank, one-sided, alpha=0.05. n=34 needed to detect Cohen's d=0.5 at 80% power; n=18 for d=0.7. Current n=8 provides ~20% power for d=0.5."
  },
  "sc_not_supported_yet_to_sc_underpowered_change_record": {
    "old_verdict": "SC_NOT_SUPPORTED_YET",
    "new_verdict": "SC_UNDERPOWERED",
    "changed_date": "2026-05-13",
    "reason": "SC_NOT_SUPPORTED_YET was applied because the pilot had n=2 valid pairs \u2014 genuinely insufficient for any test. After expansion to n=8, the test was run and returned p>0.05 for all signatures. The failure mode is now identifiable as insufficient power (n=8, ~20% power for d=0.5), not structural assay incapability. SC_UNDERPOWERED is the precise label."
  }
